# Plasm workflow

Plan from the current requirement, taught symbols and observed results. Successful execution receipts are evidence of their confirmed effects. Do not repeat a confirmed write or reread solely to reconfirm it; inspect state when a requested condition or an effect remains unresolved. Stop with no tool call when observations establish every requested effect. Intermediate results alone are not completion.

1. Open `plasm_context` with `session_mode: "new"` and the original `intent`.
2. Teaching exposes declarations, not execution authority or acquired values. Routing errors are failures. Follow prerequisites: call producers and bind outputs to consumer arguments.

4. Before writes, bind each requested selection condition and destination to observed evidence. Keep unresolved conditions explicit; do not act on those targets. Rank, count and membership in a related collection do not establish the requested predicate. Preserve source identity through joins and aggregation. Previews are incomplete: inspect full values or compute from them. Check derived values against their source and intended invariants before using them in effects. Bind verified targets and observed inputs; calculate inside the DAG. Preserve unrequested properties; distinguish identity updates from replacement. Review all effects, including dependent writes.
5. Compare observations with requested scope, effects and preserved properties. Calls establish only declared results. After call or terminal rejection, repair the unfinished requirement in-session; changing call shape alone does not complete it. Preserve the verified target set and permitted effects during recovery. A rejected operation establishes failure of that attempt, not global infeasibility. Separate the remaining requirement from the resources tried; extend discovery when available options are unresolved. After partial or unknown effects, re-read state and reconcile receipts before further writes. Check local transformations before attributing unexpected values to the service.
